278
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:20,920
If we go to court,

279
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:21,920
how can I face

280
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:23,200
both sides?

281
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:26,360
What you should face most are the facts and the truth.

282
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:30,540
You should be very familiar with this photo.

283
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:35,320
We are all parents.

284
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,840
Shouldn't we put ourselves in their shoes?

285
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:49,810
This little motorcycle can even move.

286
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:06,840
You're quite tall, sis. Are you 1.8 meters?

287
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:07,600
I'm not.

288
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:09,600
Just talk. Don't lean over here.

289
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:10,600
Move over there.

290
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:12,160
Harassing my female colleague over there.

291
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:13,200
Then sue me.

292
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:14,800
What's harassment? What's small talk?

293
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:15,760
Can't you tell?

294
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:16,880
Just throwing words around.

295
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:18,000
I think you look quite tacky.

296
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,120
Calling people 'sis' all day long.

297
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:20,520
Aren't you tacky?

298
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:22,760
Do you know what's tacky and what's trendy?

299
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:23,640
Look at your hairstyle.

300
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:24,360
I'm warning you.

301
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:25,440
Don't talk about my hairstyle.

302
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:27,400
Your hairstyle looks like parentheses. So what if I said it?

303
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:28,400
You're one to talk.

304
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:29,920
Look at your alternative mullet.

305
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:31,880
You're wearing your uncle's clothes.

306
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:32,640
My old...

307
00:12:32,640 --> 00:12:33,280
How is it?

308
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:34,520
What do you think?

309
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:35,640
Absolutely. Understood.

310
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:36,970
Let's go. Get in the car.

311
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:41,520
Lawyer Li, how did it go?

312
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:43,580
Why even ask? Look how arrogant he is.

313
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:44,880
No, no way.

314
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:46,610
I'll go in and talk to him again.

315
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:48,640
No need. Get in the car.

316
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,860
Bluetooth, help me find someone.

317
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:01,120
Your case goes to trial today, right?

318
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:06,560
Yeah, right here. I think you're a little nervous.

319
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,120
Why would I be nervous?

320
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:09,040
We've known each other for so many years.

321
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:10,880
It's not our first time being opponents.

322
00:13:10,880 --> 00:13:12,610
We've done so many mock trials.

323
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:14,920
I meant your muscles are tense.

324
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:16,690
What are you talking about?

325
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:18,930
I was talking about my muscles.

326
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,730
I've been in court a lot lately.

327
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:21,930
My jaw is a bit tight.

328
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:23,720
And my facial muscles are a bit tense.

329
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:25,640
Okay, I'll loosen you up in a bit.

330
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:28,400
How? By slapping me twice?

331
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:29,720
Relax.

332
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:31,520
Gently.

333
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:38,680
Come on.

334
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:44,280
What?

335
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:45,480
What are you looking at?

336
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:46,680
Eat your food.

337
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:48,280
So much?

338
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:49,520
I'm cheering you on.

339
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:51,000
You need a full stomach to fight well. Come on.

340
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,800
Don't show him any mercy this time.

341
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:54,880
But don't be too harsh either.

342
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:55,520
Men.

343
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:57,520
Sometimes they can't handle losing face.

344
00:13:57,520 --> 00:13:59,180
Okay, I'll fight how I should.

345
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,420
Where are the buns?

346
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:01,690
They're still warm.

347
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:02,680
I'll take them then.

348
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:03,480
What for?

349
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:04,640
Just eat them.

350
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:05,400
Eat before you go.

351
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:07,000
Be safe. Safety first.

352
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:08,160
I'm leaving.

353
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:11,290
Let's make a bet.

354
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:13,400
I'm definitely betting on Xiaolong.

355
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:14,920
Why would you bet on her?

356
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:16,800
That's your own son.

357
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:18,400
He bought you sea cucumbers for nothing.

358
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:20,260
Besides, didn't you eat them too?

359
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:23,530
I bet on Xiaoxin.

360
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:04,680
The court investigation phase is over.

361
00:15:04,680 --> 00:15:06,120
We now enter the debate phase.

362
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:10,120
First, the plaintiff's representative will present their arguments.

363
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:11,320
Your Honor.

364
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:14,480
According to the regulations promulgated by the National Financial Regulatory Administration

365
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:16,800
in the "Health Insurance Management Measures",

366
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:18,680
insurance companies shall not use diagnostic criteria

367
00:15:18,680 --> 00:15:20,880
that do not match the insurance contract as a reason

368
00:15:20,880 --> 00:15:22,480
to refuse to pay insurance benefits.

369
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:23,160
Regarding this case,

370
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:25,800
for the condition of disseminated intravascular coagulation,

371
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,440
whether it has early, middle, or late stages,

372
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:29,200
and whether a blood transfusion was required as a result,

373
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:31,120
it is all because the hospital and the insurance company have

374
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:32,480
different diagnostic criteria.

375
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:35,440
Therefore, the defendant cannot refuse to pay on this basis.

376
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:36,120
Your Honor.

377
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:37,880
The National Financial Regulatory Administration is an agency

378
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:40,240
that supervises the banking and insurance industries.

379
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:42,560
It does not have any law enforcement power.

380
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:44,880
I believe the regulations presented by the plaintiff's lawyer

381
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:47,880
are too broad in scope

382
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:49,680
to be directly used as a basis for judgment.

383
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:51,400
However, the National Financial Regulatory Administration

384
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:52,720
issued such a regulation

385
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:53,480
for a reason.

386
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:54,680
For fairness.

387
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:56,600
As we all know,

388
00:15:56,760 --> 00:15:59,040
insurance companies have so many departments,

389
00:15:59,040 --> 00:16:00,160
so many employees,

390
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:02,440
and so many top legal advisors.

391
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:04,720
They exhaust every means every day

392
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:07,040
to add various details to the policies.

393
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:09,720
A policy can have hundreds of pages.

394
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:12,800
Most of the content is obscure and difficult to understand.

395
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:15,280
It takes a law student several days to read it,

396
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:16,940
let alone an ordinary person.

397
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:19,720
They simply cannot finish reading or understand it.

398
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:22,280
Nor is it possible to get sick according to the contents of the policy.

399
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:22,920
Plaintiff.

400
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:23,400
What is DIC (disseminated intravascular coagulation)

401
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:23,960
exactly?

402
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:25,200
How many stages does DIC (disseminated intravascular coagulation)

403
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:26,040
have?

404
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:29,200
Even someone who has studied medicine has to look it up in a textbook.

405
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,080
But now,

406
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:31,800
as an ordinary person,

407
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:34,040
to get compensation from an insurance company,

408
00:16:34,040 --> 00:16:35,840
one must master this knowledge.

409
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:37,720
It's like

410
00:16:38,160 --> 00:16:40,560
a rich kid driving a sports car

411
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:43,800
wanting to race an ordinary person walking on foot.

412
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:46,920
Yes, an ordinary person would definitely lose.

413
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:49,040
But is that fair?

414
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:50,920
Your Honor,

415
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:52,280
I believe the plaintiff's lawyer

416
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:54,080
used an inappropriate example.

417
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:56,560
As a professional insurance institution,

418
00:16:56,560 --> 00:17:00,080
we serve the vast majority of ordinary people.

419
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:03,200
Every salesperson undergoes professional

420
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:05,260
and standardized pre-job training.

421
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:06,800
For every client,

422
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:08,560
we have reception videos

423
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:10,819
and after-sales follow-up recordings.

424
00:17:10,920 --> 00:17:11,800
The purpose of doing this

425
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:13,920
is precisely to make up for

426
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:17,720
the so-called unfairness raised by the plaintiff.

427
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:20,240
To borrow the plaintiff's lawyer's example,

428
00:17:20,240 --> 00:17:22,300
the company uses these requirements

429
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:26,369
to bring ordinary people into the sports car to move forward together.

430
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:29,280
What nonsense. What sports car can fit so many people?

431
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:30,120
Uncle, it's a metaphor.

432
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:30,880
Your Honor,

433
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:31,560
I know.

434
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:33,600
In response to the argument just raised by the defense,

435
00:17:33,600 --> 00:17:35,960
I request that the former salesperson who signed the insurance contract,

436
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:38,920
Li Jinwang, appear in court as a witness.

437
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:40,720
Granted.

438
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:43,120
Summon witness Li Jinwang to the court.

439
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:52,700
The plaintiff may now question the witness.

440
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:53,960
Li Jinwang,

441
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:56,800
before signing the contract, did you explain to the plaintiff,

442
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:58,320
who is my client,

443
00:17:58,400 --> 00:18:00,640
all the terms of the contract,

444
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:03,440
all the diseases, and the related restrictions?

445
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:05,600
On the day of signing,

446
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:08,120
I was explaining the contract to Mr. Han and the others,

447
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:10,600
telling them that they could ask me

448
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:12,000
about any parts they had doubts about.

449
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:12,720
But suddenly,

450
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:14,980
I received a call from my father-in-law,

451
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:16,720
saying my wife was about to give birth.

452
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:17,840
So I went out to answer the phone.

453
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:18,840
In other words,

454
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:21,600
you didn't thoroughly explain the contents of the contract

455
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,360
that day, right?

456
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:29,580
Right. After the call, I went back to the reception room

457
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:32,200
and explained the situation to Mr. Han and the others.

458
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:33,840
They congratulated me

459
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:35,500
and didn't ask anything else.

460
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,560
I signed the contract

461
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,600
and left the company.

462
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:43,220
Your Honor, I have no further questions.

463
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:44,640
Your Honor,

464
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:47,120
I also have some questions for the witness.

465
00:18:49,560 --> 00:18:52,200
Mr. Li, regarding the situation four years ago,

466
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:54,130
can you still remember it clearly?

467
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:08,000
Yes.

468
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:10,480
Because that was the day my child was born,

469
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:12,480
I remember what happened very clearly.

470
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:14,160
Could you please clarify

471
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:16,880
the parts you explained and didn't explain?

472
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:19,920
Regarding the basic parts trained by the company,

473
00:19:19,920 --> 00:19:22,000
I gave a detailed explanation at that time.

474
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,400
Next, the clients needed to

475
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,600
ask questions about the unclear parts,

476
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,360
and we would answer them.

477
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:30,720
But due to my personal reasons, this was not completed.

478
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:32,040
So, in other words,

479
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:36,440
regarding the basic contract details trained by the company,

480
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:38,280
you had already finished explaining them.

481
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:39,520
It was only when the clients wanted to

482
00:19:39,520 --> 00:19:41,640
ask further questions about their own situations

483
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:43,640
that you left the reception room, right?

484
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:44,200
Yes.

485
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:45,440
Your Honor,

486
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:47,640
I...

487
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:48,720
the video evidence from the reception room submitted earlier...

488
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:49,080
I...

489
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:49,800
the video evidence from the reception room submitted earlier,

490
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:51,840
I would like to further elaborate on it.

491
00:19:51,840 --> 00:19:53,800
Granted. Please play it.

492
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:19,480
Mr. Han.

493
00:20:20,280 --> 00:20:21,080
What's wrong?

494
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:27,440
After Mr. Li Jinwang left the reception room in the video,

495
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:29,520
the lady who came in

496
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:32,600
was also a salesperson for Shengkang Insurance at the time.

497
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:33,920
Mr. and Mrs. Han

498
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:37,000
questioned this salesperson,

499
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:39,320
and she gave a detailed answer.

500
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:40,240
Your Honor,

501
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:41,400
the video has no sound.

502
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:42,120
It cannot be proven

503
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:44,080
that the salesperson was explaining

504
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:45,600
the contract details to my client.

505
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:47,130
Counsel for the defendant,

506
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:48,200
can your salesperson

507
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:49,960
also appear in court to testify?

508
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:50,620
Your Honor,

509
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:52,760
the salesperson has resigned

510
00:20:52,760 --> 00:20:54,040
and is not in the country.

511
00:20:54,040 --> 00:20:55,840
But we have hired a lip-reading expert

512
00:20:55,840 --> 00:20:57,920
to translate the video evidence.

513
00:20:57,920 --> 00:20:59,380
And it has been notarized.

514
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:02,440
We can submit it together as supplementary evidence.

515
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:08,480
Counsel for the plaintiff, please take a look as well.

516
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:13,440
After expert analysis,

517
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:14,720
the content of this video

518
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:15,000
between the video evidence and witness testimony, exactly shows Mr. Han asking the salesperson in the surveillance video provided by the applicant.

519
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:17,400
exactly shows Mr. Han asking the salesperson

520
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:20,040
under what conditions the policy would be denied,

521
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:21,440
and she gave an answer.

522
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:24,920
If it does not meet the policy's disease restrictions,

523
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:27,200
such as severe coma resuscitation

524
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:30,240
for less than 96 hours, it will be denied.

525
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:33,520
I really forgot.

526
00:21:34,120 --> 00:21:36,600
There was too much said, and it was too complicated at the time.

527
00:21:36,600 --> 00:21:38,840
I... I really forgot.

528
00:21:46,440 --> 00:21:47,760
Our insurance company

529
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:50,280
has fulfilled its obligation to inform.

530
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:51,040
And the plaintiff,

531
00:21:51,040 --> 00:21:54,080
knowing that 96 hours of resuscitation was required

532
00:21:54,080 --> 00:21:56,000
to receive compensation,

533
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:58,440
still actively chose to give up,

534
00:21:58,640 --> 00:22:01,840
and later filed a lawsuit against the insurance company.

535
00:22:03,480 --> 00:22:06,210
This is a violation of the spirit of the contract.

536
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:09,560
We will now proceed to closing statements.

537
00:22:09,560 --> 00:22:12,290
Proceed in the order of plaintiff and defendant.

538
00:22:13,560 --> 00:22:14,640
My clients

539
00:22:15,520 --> 00:22:17,960
are parents who have just lost their child.

540
00:22:18,320 --> 00:22:19,600
Like millions of

541
00:22:19,600 --> 00:22:20,920
ordinary people,

542
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:24,120
they have no professional knowledge of medicine or insurance.

543
00:22:24,120 --> 00:22:25,680
They cannot clearly understand

544
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:28,840
under what circumstances they qualify for compensation,

545
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:31,100
or which specific conditions they meet.

546
00:22:31,160 --> 00:22:32,220
But the defendant,

547
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:34,560
a professional institution,

548
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:36,640
should have explained it in detail beforehand,

549
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:39,400
and actively contacted the clients afterwards

550
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:42,280
to identify the items and basis for compensation.

551
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:44,000
Instead of acting like this,

552
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:46,920
taking advantage of the clients' lack of knowledge

553
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:49,810
to evade responsibility and coldly reject them.

554
00:22:50,840 --> 00:22:51,560
Finally,

555
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:52,760
I would like to

556
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:55,720
address the issue repeatedly raised by the opposing counsel

557
00:22:55,720 --> 00:22:56,980
and provide an answer.

558
00:22:58,040 --> 00:23:00,000
I hope you can tell me the truth.

